# .trivyignore
# Suppress known false-positive or accepted-risk CVEs from Trivy scans.
# Format: one CVE-ID or GHSA-ID per line, with an optional comment explaining the exception.
#
# Example:
#   CVE-2023-12345  # false positive — not reachable in our build
#
# Keep this file lean. Every entry should be reviewed and re-evaluated each quarter.
# Reference: https://aquasecurity.github.io/trivy/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Trivy failure thresholds (see .github/workflows/docker-image-scan.yml)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both the `builder` and `runtime` Docker image stages are scanned.
#
#   CRITICAL  -> FAILS the build. A CRITICAL CVE cannot be merged unless it is
#                explicitly suppressed in this file (with a justification) or a
#                fix is available and applied.
#   HIGH      -> Produces a WARNING (does not fail the build) and automatically
#                opens a tracking issue so the finding is triaged and remediated.
#   MEDIUM/LOW-> Reported in the uploaded scan artefact only; no gating.
#
# Scan results (JSON/SARIF) are uploaded as CI artefacts for every run.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Review process for entries in this ignore file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Every entry MUST include a comment explaining why it is suppressed
#    (e.g. false positive, not reachable, no fix available yet).
# 2. Entries are reviewed and re-evaluated each quarter. Entries that are no
#    longer applicable (fix released, code path removed) MUST be deleted.
# 3. Suppressing a CRITICAL CVE requires sign-off from a maintainer and a
#    linked tracking issue for remediation.
# 4. Prefer upgrading the base image or dependency over adding an entry here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Suppressed CVEs (one per line, with justification)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# (none currently)